graph: {"blueprint":{"architecture_notes":"Nodes represent behavioral milestones and evals rather than technical specs.  Focus on proving the core loop works from request -> routing -> skill execution -> memory write-back.\n","major_capabilities":["Multi-client portability (Bridge)","Jev 3-tier request routing","Memory classification against the established destination map","Automated skill execution","Visual layer consolidation"],"vision":"Implement the 5-part spine of the Jev + Claude OS walkthrough: Three layers,  request routing, skill backbone, organized memory, and a shared interface.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-28","description":"A milestone metric graph focused on basic evals and honest goals for the  AgentOS core loop, bridging multiple interfaces (Obsidian, Taskdog, Zed, Terminal) into a transparently simple 3-layer system (Visual, Memory, Skills).\n","execution_policy":{"default_executor":"cursor_cli","frontier_auto_advance":true,"max_concurrent_jobs":3},"graph_version":"1.0","last_updated":"2026-09-28","nodes":[{"id":"bridge-multi-client","milestones":["A request sent from Obsidian is recorded once by the bridge.","The same request sent from a second client (Zed, Taskdog, or the terminal) is recorded by that same bridge.","Both submissions are routed to the same outcome."],"status":"ready","title":"Eval: Bridge accepts requests from multiple interfaces (Obsidian, Taskdog, Zed, Terminal)","type":"capability"},{"id":"cost-aware-model-router","milestones":["A simple lookup ('Bring up the morning brief') stays under the minimum budget threshold and executes as an instant action.","A generative request ('What was the biggest news?') triggers the fast-model budget criteria and returns a cheap, fast answer.","A complex request ('Write me an explainer') hits the escalation criteria, routes to a full agent, and logs the decision for Laya's shadow training."],"status":"ready","title":"Eval: Router enforces budget and escalation criteria to dynamically select the most cost-effective model/agent (logs decisions for Laya)","type":"capability"},{"id":"memory-layer-discipline","milestones":["Classification uses the destination map already present for this product.","The agent writes its synthesis to the agent destination that map already names.","A person can open that result from the location the map already gives."],"status":"ready","title":"Eval: Classification uses the destination map already established for this product","type":"capability"},{"id":"skill-backbone-automation","milestones":["One recurring workflow (a presence brief over social accounts, Taskdog, and daily notes) is documented so a human could follow it manually.","That same skill runs headlessly and writes its finished deliverable to the agent destination the existing map already names.","Running the skill a second time produces a new deliverable without requiring any code rewrites to the skill."],"status":"pending","title":"Goal: Convert at least one manual conversational workflow into an automated, headless skill","type":"capability"},{"id":"visual-layer-consolidation","milestones":["The presence-brief deliverable is visible on Obsidian or a lean desktop app without opening the background run.","The metrics inside the deliverable, including social accounts and GitHub commits, are fully rendered and visible.","Asking a question about the deliverable from that display reads the persistent copy the skill wrote."],"status":"pending","title":"Goal: The shared interface displays deliverables (metrics, schedules) driven by the headless skills","type":"capability"}],"nodes_dir":"nodes/","project_id":"agentos-core","project_name":"AgentOS Core Loop","repo":"local/agentos","schema_type":"project_graph","schema_version":"1.0"}

